; The one variable: a CSGMesh3D whose mesh is a TextMesh with depth. The brush builder takes the
; surface of a font-built mesh once the font loads, so the left text draws as a solid and the right
; text, subtracted from a CSGBox3D, cuts the letters out of it with walls in its own material. No
; other golden shows it: unit-csg-mesh holds meshes with no font, and unit-text-mesh draws its
; TextMesh through a MeshInstance3D. The box is taller and wider than the text, so no cut edge lies
; where the font hinting of Godot moves a glyph by a pixel.
